  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"The Moon has no weather was made possible by a grant from the Women's Studio Workshop in Rosendale, NY"--Colophon.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"The text is set in Fox designed by Chad Kloepfer and letterpress printed on Magnani Arturo. Additional papers are Thai mulberry, hand-marbled Hahnemühle Bugra, handmade abaca, acid-free paper from scientific lab books and pages from a 1984 Polish electronics manual. The cover is letterpress on board"--Colophon.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">LC has copy 27.</subfield>
    <subfield code="5">DLC</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="504" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Includes bibliographical references.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="520" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"This book features a short text by the artist drawn from scientific research on lunar geology to poetically explore the idea of the Moon as a book. Illustrations borrowed from engineering diagrams and printed on three different papers are folded into the signature to interrupt the prose and create layers of visual information. Each book includes a removable cotton casting or 'moon card' nestled in the back cover"--Women's Studio Workshop website, viewed December 14, 2021.</subfield>
  </datafield>
